-- title:
--   Global 1-forms restrict to regular differentials on ℚ̄(X₀(N))
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a prime $p$, and write $R = \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism of schemes with $X$ integral, $c$ proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$, and let $\mathcal{V}$ be a two-chart affine open cover of $X$: opens $U_0, U_1$ with $U_0 \sqcup U_1 = \top$ and $U_0$, $U_1$, $U_0 \sqcap U_1$ affine, so that $(\mathcal{V}.\mathrm{cover}\ c).A_0 = \Gamma(X, U_0)$ with its $R$-algebra structure coming from $c$. Write $\bar F_N$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the intermediate field $F_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions, viewed inside the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume given a ring homomorphism $\iota : \Gamma(X, U_0) \to \bar F_N$ which (hιR) is compatible with the structure maps, i.e. $\iota \circ (R \to \Gamma(X,U_0))$ equals $R \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \bar F_N$; (hιinj) is injective; (hιrat) has image inside the image of $F_N$ under the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb`; and (hιfrac) is birational onto it, in the sense that every $x \in F_N$ satisfies $\mathrm{coeffEmb}(x) \cdot \iota b = \iota a$ for some $a, b \in \Gamma(X, U_0)$ with $\iota b \ne 0$. Let $\mathrm{res}$ be an additive map from the degree-zero Čech cohomology $(\mathcal{V}.\mathrm{kaehlerSections}\ c).H_0$ — the kernel of the Čech differential inside the product of the two chartwise Kähler differential modules — to $\Omega_{\bar F_N / \overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$, and assume (hres) that $\mathrm{res}\,\omega$ is the image of the $U_0$-component $\omega.1$ under the semilinear map [`KaehlerDifferential.mapOfRingHom`](def/AlgebraicGeometry_TwoAffineOpenCoverKaehler.html#L16) attached to $R \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\iota$. Then for every such $\omega$, $\mathrm{res}\,\omega$ lies in `regularDifferentialsBar N`: for every place $v$ of $\bar F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ there is $f$ in the valuation subring of $v$ with $\mathrm{res}\,\omega = f \cdot v.\mathrm{dCoord}$.
--
--   This is the statement that a global relative $1$-form on a smooth proper integral $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-model of $X_0(N)$ restricts, along a birational identification of the generic fibre with the geometric modular function field, to a differential regular at every place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0(N))$. It is obtained from the corresponding field-level statement over the perfect base field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with the identification of $\bar F_N$ with the function field of the base-changed curve, and it feeds the comparison of the integral lattice of $q$-expansions with $H^0$ of the model.
